quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  28,60,And whatever things you have been given are only the (temporary) enjoyments of the life of this world and its glamour. But whatever lies with Allah is better and more lasting. Do you not then understand?
  28,61,"Can the person to whom We have given a good promise, which he will receive, be like him whom We have provided the (momentary) enjoyment in the life of this world, then, on the Day of Resurrection, he shall be among those who are summoned (to account for their deeds)?"
  28,62,"And on the Day, He will call out to them and say: ‘Where are My partners whom you used to claim?’"
  28,63,"Those (deviant leaders) against whom the decree (of torment) will be passed will say: ‘Our Lord! These (followers) are the ones whom we caused to deviate. We led them into deviance, for we were deviant ourselves. We disassociate ourselves (from them) before You. It was not us whom they worshipped. (Rather they worshipped their lusts).’"
  28,64,"It will be said (to the disbelievers): ‘Invoke your (self-made) partner-gods (for help)!’ So they will invoke them, but they will not respond to them. And they will see the punishment, wishing they had followed guidance!"
  28,65,The Day when He will call out to them and say: ‘What response did you give to the messengers?’
  28,66,"On that Day, all information shall be blacked out for them so they cannot question one another."
  28,67,"As for him who repents, believes and acts righteously, perhaps he will be among the successful."
  28,68,"And your Lord creates whatever He wishes and chooses. They have no choice. Glory be to Allah, and Exalted is He above any partners they ascribe (to Him)."
  28,69,And your Lord knows what their breasts conceal and what they reveal.
  28,70,"And He is Allah—there is no god except Him. All praise belongs to Him in this world and the Hereafter. (Final) judgement belongs to Him. And to Him, you shall be returned."
